      "id": 1,
      "text": "Eagle Lake earned its name from a small glacial lake that once covered a quarter of Section 7 and nearby swamps, supplying wild cranberries for Chicago markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_lake_illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in Eagle Lake in 1865 and closed in 1902, marking the community’s brief 37‑year federal presence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_lake_illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the late 19th century, farmers drained the original lake through ditches and tiling, shrinking it to a modest pond and converting wetlands into farmland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_lake_illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before settlers, the Potawatomi tribe inhabited the Eagle Lake area, using its prairies, woodlands, and waterways for hunting, fishing, and agriculture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_lake_illinois",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Eagle Lake enjoys a humid continental climate, with January lows near –7 °C and July highs around 29 °C, and about 41 inches of rain annually.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_lake_illinois",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Eagle Lake is part of the Chicago‑Naperville‑Elgin metropolitan statistical area, linking it to a major economic region.",
